<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- THE WINDOW COLOUR, AND IT FOLLOWS THE PHONE (owner, 2026-09-22: "jab ham
         system se light mode karte hain to app light mode mein nahin jaati hai").

         This colour has to be repeated in XML because the WINDOW is painted
         before Compose draws its first frame and the framework cannot read a
         Compose ColorScheme. It has to equal EvLightColorScheme's `background`,
         and values-night/colors.xml has to equal EvDarkColorScheme's, or the
         splash-to-Compose handover is a flash of colour rather than a change of
         content. If one of them ever moves, move both.

         Neither value is invented: #FFFFFF is PaletteTokens.Neutral100 and
         #000000 is Neutral0, both read out of the pinned material3-android-1.4.0
         jar's own bytecode.

         values-night/ IS BACK, and this is the third time it has come and gone.
         It existed from 2026-09-08 when the app followed the system, went on
         2026-09-17 when the app became black in every mode, and returns now for
         the same reason it existed the first time: with two schemes, one file
         cannot state both, and a light phone opening on a black rectangle is a
         flash. -->
    <color name="ev_background">#FFFFFFFF</color>
</resources>
